{"nodes": [{"id": "poultry_monitoring_system_backend_templates_flocks_chickentry_list_template", "label": "Flocks Chick Entry List Template", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "poultry-monitoring-system/backend/templates/flocks/chickentry_list.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "poultry_monitoring_system_backend_templates_flocks_chickentry_list_generic_list_scaffold", "label": "Generic Paginated Record List Scaffold", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "poultry-monitoring-system/backend/templates/flocks/chickentry_list.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single copy-pasted list template body (search form on GET 'q', table over object_list rendering str(obj) plus created_at, an empty-state block, and an included pagination partial) is reused verbatim across flocks, health, inventory and iot apps. The trade-off is deliberate: it lets every model get a working CRUD list page with no per-model template work, at the cost of showing only the model's __str__ instead of domain columns, so any screen that needs real columns must be forked into a bespoke template."}, {"id": "poultry_monitoring_system_backend_templates_flocks_chickentry_list_url_name_derived_title", "label": "URL-Name Derived Page Title", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "poultry-monitoring-system/backend/templates/flocks/chickentry_list.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Page heading and title are computed at render time from request.resolver_match.url_name with the '_list' suffix cut and title-cased, so one shared template self-labels for every route that renders it. This is what makes the generic list scaffold reusable without a per-view context variable, but it couples display text to URL naming conventions."}], "edges": [{"source": 